@@ -388,9 +388,49 @@
 
 ### Don't:
 
-- **Don't** put white text on #fe6e35 or any lighter orange; use the darker action token for readable text.
+- **Don't** put white text on #f47932 or any lighter orange; use the darker action token for readable text.
 - **Don't** convey risk or status by color alone, and don't paraphrase or abbreviate a status label.
 - **Don't** wrap sections inside a surface in tinted boxes; Apricot tint means open, hovered or current.
 - **Don't** unmask names, phone numbers or national IDs in list or card views, or use real personal data in screenshots.
 - **Don't** introduce a second accent hue for headings or primary actions; the clinical blue belongs to the in-progress status family only.
 - **Don't** add shadows inside work surfaces or drawers other than an open menu.
+
+
+## Orange and white navigation (15 October 2026)
+
+The primary brand is exactly #f47932. Staff navigation uses this solid orange with
+#342014 text; the current destination uses a white surface and action ink. The
+organization selector sits on apricot. Content remains on white work surfaces,
+with a warm neutral canvas. Primary buttons use #c45428 with white text for AA
+contrast. Teal, blue and sage distinguish data series; clinical statuses retain
+their labels and semantic colors. Long navigation labels wrap, sidebar controls
+have 44px targets, and reduced-motion preferences disable sidebar transitions.
+
+
+## All routed surfaces (15 October 2026)
+
+The orange/white system applies to the entire app: landing and clinic picker,
+staff and patient sign-in, registration and recovery, help and clinic details,
+legal/error pages, assessment questions/results/history, and every hospital,
+school and system administration workspace. Public navigation is white with
+orange actions; public hero imagery stays visible through a light warm overlay.
+Account introductions use apricot with dark ink instead of navy. Staff navigation
+uses the exact brand orange. The footer uses deep ink for a quiet endpoint.
+
+Use `--suth-accent: #f47932` for brand regions with `--suth-on-accent` ink;
+`--suth-action` remains the readable white-text action. Every public and staff
+control receives a visible focus indication. Covered mobile admin content is
+inert; Escape closes the drawer and returns focus to the menu button. Keyboard
+skip links lead to main work areas. Long Thai labels wrap before clipping.
+
+Medical scores, chart categories and explicitly authored assessment themes retain
+their meaning; action buttons do not inherit arbitrary risk colors. Missing BMI
+or scores are described as missing rather than interpreted as a medical result.
+Assessment questions expose programmatic labels, grouped choices and linked
+validation errors. Card navigation uses native links/buttons.
+
+Verification evidence lives under `../outputs/all-pages-ui/`: per-route desktop
+and mobile accessibility inventories, screenshots, school organization variants
+and populated-question checks. Responsive coverage additionally exercises 320px,
+900px, 1440px, landscape dialogs and a bounded 2560px workspace. These checks use
+synthetic fixtures and do not certify live-service or physical-device behavior.
